# Luminary — V2i theme-picker seed
- date: 2026-09-27
- branch: fix/cli-254-v2i-theme-picker-seed
- lead: alan-cooper
- supporting: [michael-feathers, saltzer-schroeder]

## Cooper (lead) — operator experience
The V2i drives simulate an operator running `/onboard-repo` or `/launch`
in a fresh workspace. A fresh workspace where the picker fires is not the
operator's real experience — most operators run Claude on a persistent
machine where they picked a theme once. Seeding a theme in the harness
image matches that real operator state, not a first-boot corner case.

## Feathers (supporting) — characterization
The seed is a characterization anchor. It pins the harness environment
to a shape that matches how Claude runs on the operator's machine. If a
future Claude release adds a second onboarding gate, the drive.log
diffs will show it; the seed does not hide that signal, only the theme
one.

## Saltzer-Schroeder (supporting) — least common mechanism
The seed is scoped to the Docker image's adopter user. It does not
change any global state, adopter-observable substrate, or bassclef
config. Failure blast radius: harness image only.
